    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Wolof-led confederation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#senegambia">Senegambia</a>, uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#waalo">Waalo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cayor">Cayor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#baol">Baol</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-sine">Sine</a> and Saloum under an overlord called the buurba.</li><li>It linked the interior with the Atlantic coast just as Portuguese traders arrived, and spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#wolof">Wolof</a> language across the region.</li><li>Atlantic wealth let coastal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vassal">vassals</a> break away; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cayor">Cayor</a>'s victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-danki">Danki</a> c. 1549 ended Jolof's imperial phase.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1488 the exiled Jolof prince Bemoim was received and baptised at the court of King Joao II in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lisbon">Lisbon</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

